0,Cajun music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cajun_music,"Cajun music (French: Musique cadienne) is a traditional genre of music from Louisiana. An emblematic music of Louisiana played by the Cajuns, it is rooted in the ballads of the French-speaking Acadians of Canada.","French, Cajun",Indo-European
1,History of Cajun music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Cajun_music,"History of Cajun music Cajun musicians at a 2010 Courir de Mardi Gras Cajun music has its roots based in the ballads of the French-speaking Acadians of Canada, and in country music.","French, Cajun",Indo-European
2,Cajun Music: About the Genre - Ballad of America,https://balladofamerica.org/cajun-music/,"Cajun music is a distinctive form of American music that blends French Acadian, German, Spanish, African American, Afro-Creole, Scottish, Irish, and English folk traditions.","French, Cajun",Indo-European
